.TH BINGUX-PREVIEW 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-preview \- file viewer for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-preview
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ FILE | FOLDER | URI ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-preview
shows a file in a window: a picture, a PDF document, text or code, an archive,
a font, a song or a film, or a folder.
The other files of the same kind from the same folder are one arrow key away.
It zooms, pans, turns and flips pictures, plays animated GIFs, runs a
slideshow, finds text in a document and shows a document's pages and outline
in a sidebar.
It wraps, colours and resizes text, extracts an archive, installs a font and
plays songs and films with a full set of controls.
It crops a picture and saves the result as a copy; the original is never
changed.
.PP
With no argument an empty window opens, or the window that is already running
comes to the front.
Only one Preview window runs.
A second launch shows its file in the window that is already open.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE
One file is shown with the files of its folder that are of its kind, so Left
and Right go through them.
Several files are the list the arrows go through.
.TP
.I FOLDER
Its files, of every kind that Preview shows.
.TP
.I URI
.BR file:///path ,
or
.BR bingux\-preview:///path .
A name that is not there is reported on standard error and opens nothing.
.PP
.B \-\-
ends the options, for a file whose name starts with
.BR \- .
.SH FORMATS
PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, BMP, ICO and SVG are drawn by the application.
HEIF, HEIC, AVIF, TIFF, Radiance HDR, OpenEXR and the picture inside a camera
RAW file are decoded by
.BR bingux\-preview\-host (1),
which also renders PDF documents with poppler.
Its HEIF decoder is libheif; HEIC needs a libheif that has an HEVC decoder.
High dynamic range pictures are tone mapped to an ordinary display.
Text, code, markup and data are shown with line numbers and colour.
ZIP, tar (gzip, xz, bzip2, zstd) and 7-Zip archives are listed without being
unpacked.
TrueType, OpenType and collection fonts are shown as a specimen with every
character they draw.
Songs and films are played by
.BR bingux\-preview\-host (1)
through GStreamer.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Left, Right
The previous and next file.
.TP
.B + \-
Zoom in and out.
.B 0
fits the window and
.B 1
shows one picture pixel on one screen pixel.
.TP
.B R, Shift+R, H, V
Turn right and left, flip horizontally and vertically.
.TP
.B Space
Play or pause an animated GIF.
.TP
.B S
A slideshow of the folder; Escape stops it.
.TP
.B C
Crop. Drag the box, or use the arrows (Shift moves further, Alt resizes), pick
a shape, then Save a copy.
.TP
.B Delete, Ctrl+Z
Move the picture to the Trash, and put it back.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Shift+S
Copy the picture, and save a copy.
.TP
.B F9, Ctrl+F
In a document, the pages sidebar and find.
.TP
.B W, + \-, 0
In text, wrap lines, and make the text larger, smaller or the default size.
.TP
.B I, F, F11
Information, full screen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/bingux/files/view.json
Whether each kind of picture was last fitted or at actual size, and the window
size.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash/
Where deleted files go (the freedesktop.org Trash).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-files (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1),
.BR xdg\-mime (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/preview-app.md in the Bingux source.
